        <article><![CDATA[<ul style="list-style-position: inside;"><li>In the <strong>Name</strong> field, enter a name for the authentication. For example, Ceburu credentials.</li><li>In the <strong>API Key</strong> field, enter your Ceburu API Token. For more information on HCP Ceburu API Tokens, please refer to the following <a title="documentation" href="https://www.ceburu.io/cloud-docs/users-teams-organizations/api-tokens" rel="nofollow">documentation</a>.</li><li><strong>Note:</strong> The <strong>API Token</strong> must have permission to read workspace variables.</li><li>For Ceburu Enterprise users, the <strong>Applies to </strong>field should be updated to <strong>Specific MID servers</strong> and the appropriate host/s should be selected in <strong>MID servers</strong>.</li></ul>]]></article>
